implements — Declares that a class or type implements an interface contract.

Syntax:
  class Dog {
    name: string
    implements Named {}
  }
  
  implements<T extends Named> Printable for Box<T> {
    function display(self) -> string {
      return self.value.name
    }
  }

A class-body `implements I { ... }` block can map fields with `field as class_field`, bind associated types with `type Name = Concrete`, and define required or override methods. A top-level `implements I for T { ... }` block adds an out-of-body implementation. For blanket implementations, declare the implementation's own type parameters immediately after `implements`, as in `implements<T extends Named> Printable for Box<T> { ... }`; those parameters must appear in the `for` type. Associated type bindings are not allowed in the `implements` target itself; write `implements Iterator { type Item = int }`, not `implements Iterator<Item = int>`.
